## 🔒 Security Notes

- All Supabase queries use the **anon key** but are protected by **Row Level Security (RLS)** policies
- A user can only read/write their own data
- Embedded chat page (`/embed/:chatbotId`) uses the same Supabase auth — customer visitors must be signed in as anonymous users or a shared account
- Rate limiting on the AI backend is IP-based (in-memory, resets on server restart)
- The Groq API key is stored server-side only, never exposed to the browser

---

## 📡 Complete API / Supabase Call Summary

### Auth Calls (`supabase.auth.*`)
- `signInWithPassword` — Login
- `signUp` — Register
- `signOut` — Logout
- `getSession` — Check session
- `getUser` — Get current user
- `onAuthStateChange` — Real-time session listener
- `updateUser({ data: {...} })` — Update profile metadata
- `updateUser({ password })` — Change password

### Database Calls (`supabase.from(table).*`)
| Table | Operations Used |
|---|---|
| `chatbots` | SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE |
| `conversations` | SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE |
| `messages` | SELECT, INSERT |
| `faqs` | SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE |
| `workflows` | SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE |

### External HTTP
- `POST http://localhost:3001/api/chat` — Groq AI response (from `ChatInterface`)
